From d0c0f0db3596ffaa4894fad4cdf7b3ed12c49881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 08:21:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 5: control *Renderer classes + VisualStyles state enums

Adds the eleven visual-style control renderers and the twelve VisualStyles state
enums they consume. Signatures and enum values taken from the net48 reference.

VisualStyles state enums (System.Windows.Forms.VisualStyles): PushButtonState,
CheckBoxState, RadioButtonState, ComboBoxState, GroupBoxState,
ScrollBarArrowButtonState, ScrollBarSizeBoxState, ScrollBarState, TabItemState,
TextBoxState, TrackBarThumbState, EdgeStyle.

Renderers (System.Windows.Forms): ButtonRenderer, CheckBoxRenderer,
RadioButtonRenderer, GroupBoxRenderer, ComboBoxRenderer, TextBoxRenderer,
TabRenderer, ProgressBarRenderer, ScrollBarRenderer, TrackBarRenderer. Unlike the
ToolStripRenderer chrome (which GTK draws for live controls), these are called by
owner-draw code to draw INTO a caller-supplied Graphics, so they render real
(classic, non-themed) output via ControlPaint/TextRenderer rather than being
no-ops - a documented visual deviation from Windows visual styles.

Full suite green at 2317 (+2 tests: size/support constants, and a smoke test that
draws with every renderer into an off-screen bitmap without throwing).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
